This chapter highlights the concern for the ductile behavior of ships and offshore structures and their structural components under ultimate conditions. It discusses the influence of fabrication imperfections and in-service damage and degradation on reserve strength. Uncertainties in strength models for design are also highlighted. It also reviews the latest literature on the development of both empirical and analytical methods. The method of thermovision, using high-resolution infrared cameras, is promising a part of hull surveillance systems. High speed vessels are designed for some special load conditions and the elastic buckling limit of frames, decks may be of special interest and not only the ultimate strength. The initial imperfections used in the committee member models are generated subjecting first the panel to pure lateral pressure on the smooth plate side, and then keeping the resulting displacement pattern as the stress free imperfection. The study of heat-affected zone (HAZ) is of particular importance for aluminum alloy of this type, and a parametric study of the kind carried out is very useful. All members have carried out non-linear analysis of the benchmark examples using recognized commercial Finite Element Analysis Software programs. Analysis is also done to assess the effect of the variation of yield stress in the HAZ on the ultimate strength.}
