abstract = {Publisher Summary
This chapter focuses on the design tools currently used in shipyards that are mature. The amount of work carried out by the Information Technology (IT) tools varies from 60% to 100% depending on the design phase and the shipyard. Decision support provides the designer with methods to find optimal solutions, as the charge of an innovative structure of previous projects is limited. New techniques as virtual reality are now available in the ship design offices. Ship design is a typical collaborative work leading to concurrent engineering. IT is widely used not only within the shipyard, but also with sub-contracting companies and suppliers. The various partners involved in the design tools development—shipyards, software vendors, classification societies, and research centers—have clearly identified that the real challenge for the future is still dealing with data exchange. A ship remains a very complex product with many systems and a large and complicated arrangement. A 3D model available from the early design stage helps reduce fastidious time-consuming and error-generating tasks and modifies and makes consistent overall process up to detailed design.}
