year = {2003},
isbn = {978-0-08-044076-7},
doi = {https://doi.org/10.1016/B978-008044076-7/50012-X},
url = {https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/B978008044076750012X},
abstract = {Publisher Summary
This chapter emphasizes the application of risk assessment, which has evolved over 20 years in the offshore industry and within the last 5 years in the marine industry. The offshore industry has focused on the application of risk assessment to evaluate the safety of individual offshore constructions. The marine industry primarily focuses on the applications of risk assessment, to further enhance and bring greater clarity to the international rule making process. In recent years, there has been an increase activity in the use of risk based approaches for the development of rules/regulations and standards and designs for ships. Two of the most interesting challenges are the area of risk acceptance criteria and its application within the marine industry in a consistent fashion and taking into consideration, the uncertainty in the risk modeling. It should be recognized that the analytical results of risk based approaches have a level of uncertainty. Techniques to deal with such uncertainty should also be developed.}
}
